# The image build context is the repo root, because one shared deploy/Dockerfile builds every
# service and needs `<service>/build/libs/`. Everything else is excluded — an unfiltered context
# here is the whole repo including nine Gradle caches and the ELK data.
#
# Docker's .dockerignore (unlike .gitignore) honours a `!` re-include even when a parent pattern
# excluded it, so the allowlist below works.
*

!*/build/libs/*.jar
# bootJar produces two artifacts; -plain.jar is the thin one with no dependencies and no
# Main-Class. Copying both would make the wildcard COPY ambiguous and boot the wrong one.
*/build/libs/*-plain.jar
